---
import Operations from "../../layouts/Operations.astro";
import "../../styles/release-wizard.css";
---
<Operations title="Release studio." accent="Ready for the world." description="Turn an approved package into a signed release. One clear step at a time." section="releases">
<p id="release-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Checking operator access…</p>
<section id="release-wizard" hidden>
 <ol class="release-steps" aria-label="Publication steps"><li><span>01</span> Your signing backup</li><li><span>02</span> Review the release</li><li><span>03</span> Sign &amp; publish</li></ol>
 <section class="release-step"><div class="release-step-header"><span class="step-label">01 / SIGNING</span><h2>Your seal of approval.</h2><p>Signing happens on this device. Only public signatures go to Exchange.</p></div>
 <p id="release-trust-state" class="service-note"></p>
 <details id="release-create"><summary>First time? Create a signing backup</summary><p>Create this once for your registry. Keep the encrypted backup and its password somewhere safe; you’ll need them for future releases and renewals. This setup uses separate keys for the four signing roles.</p><div class="release-form-grid"><div class="form-field"><label for="release-new-password">Backup password · at least 12 characters</label><input id="release-new-password" type="password" autocomplete="new-password" maxlength="1024" /></div><div class="form-field"><label for="release-repeat-password">Repeat password</label><input id="release-repeat-password" type="password" autocomplete="new-password" maxlength="1024" /></div></div><button class="button" id="release-generate" type="button">Create &amp; download backup</button><p>Next, reopen the downloaded file below. This checks that your backup works before you use it.</p></details>
 <div class="release-unlock"><h3>Open your signing backup</h3><p>Select the encrypted file on your device. The file and password stay in this tab.</p><input id="release-backup-file" type="file" accept=".json,application/json" hidden /><button class="button secondary" id="release-choose" type="button">Choose backup file</button><span id="release-filename">No file chosen</span><div class="form-field"><label for="release-password">Backup password</label><input id="release-password" type="password" autocomplete="off" maxlength="1024" /></div><button class="button" id="release-unlock" type="button">Unlock on this device</button><button class="button secondary" id="release-lock" type="button" hidden>Lock backup</button></div>
 <div id="release-root" hidden><h3>Your public trust file</h3><p>This file lets Tabs recognise your registry. It contains public keys only.</p><button class="button secondary" id="release-download-root" type="button">Download root.json</button><p>SHA-256 fingerprint</p><code id="release-root-hash"></code><button class="button secondary" id="release-copy-pin" type="button">Copy fingerprint</button>
 <form id="release-register" hidden novalidate><h3>Confirm your registry’s first trust root</h3><p>This permanently binds the registry’s initial signing identity. It does not publish a package. You cannot replace this root with another backup through this wizard.</p><div class="form-field"><label for="release-confirm-origin">Type the registry address shown below</label><p id="release-origin"></p><input id="release-confirm-origin" autocomplete="off" /></div><div class="form-field"><label for="release-confirm-pin">Paste the fingerprint shown above</label><input id="release-confirm-pin" autocomplete="off" maxlength="64" /></div><button class="button" type="submit">Register this trust root</button></form></div>
 </section>
 <section class="release-step"><span class="step-label">02 / RELEASE PLAN</span><h2>See exactly what goes live.</h2><p>All currently approved versions are included. Previously published approved versions stay available; revoked versions are removed from the signed list.</p><button class="button secondary" id="release-load" type="button" disabled>Load approved releases</button><ul id="release-targets" class="release-targets"></ul><p id="release-plan-status" role="status"></p></section>
 <section class="release-step"><span class="step-label">03 / PUBLICATION</span><h2>Make it official.</h2><p>The server checks signatures, review status, and the exact package files again. Nothing becomes public until those checks pass.</p><label class="release-confirm"><input id="release-confirm" type="checkbox" /> I have reviewed every package in the plan and want to publish this signed release.</label><button class="button" id="release-publish" type="button" disabled>Sign &amp; publish release</button><p id="release-result" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></section>
 <section id="release-done" class="release-step" hidden><span class="step-label">YOUR NEXT STEP</span><h2>A signed release. Ready to find.</h2><p>The registry has published your release. Check its listing, then connect your Tabs desktop to the public trust file to install it.</p><div id="release-listings"></div><a class="button secondary" href="/extensions">Browse extensions ↗</a><button class="button secondary" id="release-download-connection" type="button">Download desktop connection settings</button><p>Desktop trust is configured separately from the catalog. The downloaded file contains the registry address and public trust fingerprint. Follow the connection guide to launch Tabs with these settings.</p><a href="/docs/extensions#manually-installing-from-a-trusted-exchange">Desktop connection guide ↗</a><p>Signed updates expire: refresh timestamp metadata within 24 hours, snapshot metadata within 7 days, and targets within 30 days. Return here and sign a fresh plan using the same backup. Root rotation is required before its one-year expiry.</p></section>
</section>
</Operations>
<script>import "../../scripts/release-wizard";</script>
